== A. worked numbers.  Every row starts again from 'X -> v told once by a teller of reliability 0.3'. ==
   scenario                                                       | DESIGN (§1, §2.5, §4)      | CORRECTED
   a  first hearing                                               | f=1.00 c=0.231 e=0.615 | f=1.00 c=0.231 e=0.615
   b  + 3 other true statements about X by the same teller        | f=0.38 c=0.442 e=0.446 | f=1.00 c=0.231 e=0.615
   c  + the same teller repeats it 9 more times                   | f=1.00 c=0.750 e=0.875 | f=1.00 c=0.291 e=0.646
   d  + a second, independent teller says it once                 | f=1.00 c=0.375 e=0.688 | f=1.00 c=0.375 e=0.688
   e  + one own sighting that confirms                            | f=1.00 c=0.565 e=0.783 | f=1.00 c=0.565 e=0.783
   f  + one own sighting that contradicts (refinement, no deletion) | f=0.23 c=0.565 e=0.348 | f=0.23 c=0.565 e=0.348
   g  + the same teller DENIES it once ('X not v')                | f=1.00 c=0.375 e=0.688 | f=0.50 c=0.261 e=0.500
      (design: the denial contains v, so it is booked as a second assertion; corrected: n- += 1 on the
       teller's own slot, by an absence event or a learned exclusion)
   h  + rule from 6 OTHER members seen with v (X itself not seen) | f=1.00 c=0.767 e=0.884 | f=1.00 c=0.231 e=0.945
   i    ... then X is SEEN once not to be v (exception), m = 6    | f=0.69 c=0.828 e=0.655 | f=0.23 c=0.565 e=0.534
   j    ... seen twice not to be v, m = 6                         | f=0.57 c=0.853 e=0.559 | f=0.13 c=0.697 e=0.372
   h  + rule from 600 OTHER members seen with v (X itself not seen) | f=1.00 c=0.997 e=0.998 | f=1.00 c=0.231 e=0.999
   i    ... then X is SEEN once not to be v (exception), m = 600  | f=1.00 c=0.997 e=0.993 | f=0.23 c=0.565 e=0.565
   j    ... seen twice not to be v, m = 600                       | f=0.99 c=0.997 e=0.990 | f=0.13 c=0.697 e=0.394
   in rows h-j the corrected c is the conviction LIVED about X itself; what the category adds is the base rate
   b of the expectation (0.929 for m = 6, 0.999 for m = 600) and its own conviction S/(S+k_g) = 0.857 / 0.998.

== B. invariants ==
   1. order independence.  One tie, the same ten moments (5 with v, 5 without) in three orders:
      +++++-----   design f = 0.576  e = 0.568   |   corrected f = 0.500  e = 0.500
      +-----++++   design f = 0.666  e = 0.646   |   corrected f = 0.500  e = 0.500
      +-+-+-+-+-   design f = 0.600  e = 0.589   |   corrected f = 0.500  e = 0.500
   2. a world of 4875 experiences (evm_s1 D): the same experiences in a random order give beliefs that
      differ by at most 0.0e+00.
      retracting one told experience = decrementing its raw counters = the life without it (exact by
      construction: integer counts; the retraction moved the largest belief by 0.025 and trust,
      completeness and base rate were recomputed from the counts, not patched).
   3. conviction from one source is bounded by its reliability:  n assertions by a teller of reliability rho
      rho = 0.3:  c = 0.2308, 0.2913, 0.2999, 0.3000   (n = 1, 10, 1e3, 1e6;  bound 0.3)
      rho = 0.6:  c = 0.3750, 0.5660, 0.5996, 0.6000   (n = 1, 10, 1e3, 1e6;  bound 0.6)
      rho = 0.9:  c = 0.4737, 0.8257, 0.8992, 0.9000   (n = 1, 10, 1e3, 1e6;  bound 0.9)
   4. no return path: a category whose only member is X gives X nothing (rule without X is empty):
      corrected: c = 0.500, e = 0.750 (own evidence only)   |   design: W_eff = 1 + lambda*min(1,cap) = 1.5, c = 0.600, e = 0.800
